 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 505374,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Perform  the following operation: <span data-math=\"8\\sqrt {10}  \\times 3\\sqrt 2\">8\\sqrt {10}  \\times 3\\sqrt 2</span>.",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p><span data-math=\"8\\sqrt {10}  \\times \\left( {3\\sqrt 2 } \\right)\"></span></p>\n<p>Step 1: Multiply the rational part.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"8 \\times 3 = 24\"></span></p>\n<p>Step 2: If necessary, reduce the result of Step 1 to lowest terms.</p>\n<p>Not necessary.</p>\n<p>Step 3: Multiply the irrational parts.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"\\sqrt {10}  \\times {\\rm{ }}\\sqrt 2 {\\rm{ }} = {\\rm{ }}\\sqrt {20} \"></span></p>\n<p>Step 4: If necessary, reduce the result from Step 3 to lowest terms.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"\\sqrt {20}  = \\sqrt 4 \\sqrt 5  = 2\\sqrt 5 \"></span></p>\n<p>Step 5: The result is the product of the rational and the irrational parts.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"24\\left( {2\\sqrt 5 } \\right) = 48\\sqrt 5 \"></span></p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"48\\sqrt 5\">48\\sqrt 5</span>"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
